cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use or adapt the AI Use Case Registry, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "AI Use Case Registry"
abstract: >-
  An adoptable AI use case registry for the gambling sector. A short screening
  classifies each AI use case by its potential impact on players into one of three
  documentation tiers, and the registry collects the documentation that tier
  requires. Front end only; organizations run it on their own infrastructure.
authors:
  - name: "AiR Hub, International Gaming Institute, University of Nevada, Las Vegas"
    website: "https://www.igiairhub.com/"
repository-code: "https://github.com/IGIAirhub/ai-use-case-registry"
url: "https://www.igiairhub.com/ai-use-case-registry/"
license:
  - Apache-2.0
  - CC-BY-4.0
keywords:
  - AI governance
  - AI transparency
  - AI registry
  - gambling
  - responsible gambling
  - risk classification
